From: hisamiii <265242552+hisamiii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] loom : split an intake's records over its members

LOOM_EXP_INTAKE_SPLIT=1: an intake's members take the memory-tile stage ring's records in turn (member m: m, m + n,
...), each drained as soon as it lands, each with its own free lock (the fill writes in order, the members
drain apart); LOOM_EXP_INTAKE_STAGE_DEPTH=N: the stage ring holds N records. Intake
siblings: a second receiver of a W multicast shares its member's drain (core descriptors and lock pair only), and a
multicast member's panel resolves through its source. LOOM_EXP_ROUTE_DUMP prints routed lanes and intake rejections.
---
